  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(a,\\) \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) are positive integers less than \\(10,\\) then \\((10a+b)(10a+c)\\) equals \\(100a(a+1)+bc\\) if:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(b+c=10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(b=c\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(a+b=10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(a=b\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(a+b+c=10\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Expanding and canceling \\(100a^2+bc\\) from both sides leaves \\[ 10a(b+c)=100a. \\] Since \\(a\\) is positive, this is equivalent to \\(b+c=10.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Expand both sides and cancel their common terms",
        "The only unmatched terms are \\(10a(b+c)\\) and \\(100a\\)"
      ],
